          "question": "type 1 here, been sick all day, meter says 24 and the ketone strip went dark purple, my breath smells odd",
          "answer": "**Get emergency medical help now. Call your emergency number or go to the nearest emergency department. Don't wait to see if it passes.**\n\nYour combination of signs matches warning signs in the diabetes emergency guidance (red-flag-diabetic-emergency). That guidance lists nausea, vomiting, or abdominal pain, and breath with a fruity or acetone smell, as signs of very high blood sugar that can be life-threatening. It says these can develop over hours to days. You have been sick all day, your meter reads 24, and your ketone strip is dark purple, which is a high ketone reading. Please don't rely on the automated check that rated this \"routine.\" It did not match your description to the list, and that is not a clearance.\n\nIf you can, have someone with you, and tell the emergency team you have type 1 diabetes, your readings, and that you've been vomiting or unwell. Don't drive yourself.\n\nThe sources I can access don't say what to do at home in this situation, and they don't give doses. The sick-day guidance (lifestyle-type-2-diabetes-adherence) says illness raises blood sugar, and that medication should not simply be stopped when someone is not eating. It recommends a sick-day plan agreed in advance with your own clinician. Get medical care first, then ask your diabetes team about that plan.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
